                <pb facs="0315" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg231"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ehrman to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1903</hi>.</date><lb/>(Received 9.50 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Uprising occurred to-night, 6; no bloodshed. Army and navy officials taken
                    prisoners. Government will be organized to-night, consisting three consuls, also
                    cabinet. Soldiers changed. Supposed same movement will be effected in Colon.
                    Order prevails so far. Situation serious. Four hundred soldiers landed Colon
                    to-day Barranquilla.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ehrman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
